    The Cistercian monk Guillaume Deguileville wrote an influential dream vision in the mid-fourteenth century in which a monk attempted to reach the heavenly city of Jerusalem by walking there on foot. Although he received divine assistance, he also managed to get lost. His first big mistake occurs before he really starts his journey as he takes the advice of Leisure to abandon the path of hard work and finds himself falling deeper and deeper into sin.
